{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_00ef1fa849729e7a115af31d85fd43cd1fb0031427e120f1f4efca65a9467d02","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"memorax-ai/memorax-code@1525c20fbcad snapshot 916cf8e021cf3d6f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5b6a0e0c080d93e85bc48440fb7b4af549e7b06f580ff12e163d1ddba6deeb26"],"source_ids":["src_acab5a616cbc5342920196d674bce990"],"text":"Memory is divided into four categories: Coding Memory (engineering lessons), Repo Memory (repository knowledge), Personal Memory (user preferences), and Procedure Memory (reusable task steps).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_240adc51d6340123da53373e82062821f0b3eac1fd436951d486d551c7b93822","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"memorax-ai/memorax-code@1525c20fbcad snapshot 916cf8e021cf3d6f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7ccc2f712224f21956ba56e63a3cef34e525dd2d3a1edcbf2ad6b72538188c79","slc_e3f04685270cf484fadde12f4911ccb11a6ca1aebb0837621691cf116d9f6930"],"source_ids":["src_acab5a616cbc5342920196d674bce990"],"text":"The product targets the problem that new coding-agent sessions start without prior architecture knowledge, failed attempts, repository rules, or working preferences, providing a shared memory layer across supported clients.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2799c9f6f086415b6b0a5f59ed65bdede1342f137fd7f8f58fdd0c7e1af1c0ae","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"memorax-ai/memorax-code@1525c20fbcad snapshot 916cf8e021cf3d6f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_054433d81306f9e4994532b14f9e9c680ed2605a4f33963572a405f9929a660d"],"source_ids":["src_4075b6c35e0f503fac600b7ee3dc8a2f"],"text":"Automatic Search on turn-start Hooks is disabled by default; the usual retrieval path is the client invoking memorax-cli through the shared Skill, while Hooks still provide identity, scope, and writeback coordination.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_33c49998aa682dd0b060d2ac0b03789410322cce02f10502e48299c9b766fc10","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"memorax-ai/memorax-code@1525c20fbcad snapshot 916cf8e021cf3d6f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7900528e3333855ab5e0356863ac034b3545f90c3541b81d6fc1e8e16622f740"],"source_ids":["src_4075b6c35e0f503fac600b7ee3dc8a2f"],"text":"Adapter Hooks and plugins communicate with the Backend via versioned, client-qualified local HTTP commands carrying JSON and token headers, with a request deadline and optional cancellation; the transport does not retry or start the Backend.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4db40c8d6b9342e787b37f5653b3f25f3dd0ce716d22e502bac1edf1c8baf3a6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"memorax-ai/memorax-code@1525c20fbcad snapshot 916cf8e021cf3d6f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_97bf1f14eba071c8e88c5a666bf2b090eb3432f627bc419f008447d11c0eff63","slc_bd6ea307481ed01f1ec50a11c8815d32daec2dc623576a5cc535422eaa8eb105"],"source_ids":["src_4075b6c35e0f503fac600b7ee3dc8a2f"],"text":"After setup, the managed Backend schedules a detached updater that locks, resolves a channel target, installs an exact published version via the package-replacement path, and reuses non-interactive setup reconciliation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_66c97585ac8a651a827302d786cec72fe60923a46c914bfe5b1e9d16e5d90c54","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"memorax-ai/memorax-code@1525c20fbcad snapshot 916cf8e021cf3d6f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_03681275321475c957f26a7e5c1b3173c96675001696e6f7cdf33360c5bb98b1","slc_5be8e0e40fb4dad2e094eaeaf4ad8503b51883f97bcec0951fb67d41e45f2982"],"source_ids":["src_4075b6c35e0f503fac600b7ee3dc8a2f"],"text":"The system integrates seven coding clients with one local Backend, a capability-oriented modular monolith, surrounded by six client deployment adapters, a shared runtime source layer, and an npm assembly/CLI layer.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6a09ff5d063ad441a6116c83ff33e5750b49f3acfc6a16a9225f1e97e4c3b3e3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"memorax-ai/memorax-code@1525c20fbcad snapshot 916cf8e021cf3d6f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a6edc68a349ed51fc4b575d84d88c4fb0e2db4bb44e68a84a4d5271a65d5c361"],"source_ids":["src_acab5a616cbc5342920196d674bce990"],"text":"Local trace capture is on by default for supported clients and retained traces under MEMORAX_CODE_HOME may include prompts, responses, recalled memory, reminder text, and local paths; it can be switched to metadata-only or disabled.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6e76580d4a2d5f02c2872490438c8d5dd3af395e3f83599b0b98ede8ba8bf69b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"memorax-ai/memorax-code@1525c20fbcad snapshot 916cf8e021cf3d6f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_fb8e5bfec5e5b8458a1a6a597e36de4841d93994efcb86455239e5592ebeb207"],"source_ids":["src_acab5a616cbc5342920196d674bce990"],"text":"Personal and Procedure Memory stay in the current repository under .repo_memory/; writes compare existing content so equivalent requests make no change and conflicts update or supersede entries.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_74376d914b1cfd1da92279991a398dc08c40b9d10f10db9e750b238ffd11797c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"memorax-ai/memorax-code@1525c20fbcad snapshot 916cf8e021cf3d6f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_cef46135aedd93bc0d236be6c5dfeb7e118f2debdd8df01078fbb2cd6d6f5aa3"],"source_ids":["src_4075b6c35e0f503fac600b7ee3dc8a2f"],"text":"The Backend owns the local memory service, repository scope, trace, lifecycle, and update scheduling, but must not own model execution, provider credentials, or native transcript creation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_dedbb3ef52a30450ea7d4107a30759a1d7326e42ad2b0a8731b9af85351d99f2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"memorax-ai/memorax-code@1525c20fbcad snapshot 916cf8e021cf3d6f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2b6645c89e29fbe5103d95f97c7ce870bbc2837cd701366a24b0b974102d8922","slc_cdc9c7cf2ea4d4fbbc152d671708fb99b6161391e538b5e1a1061c7b0b2a9c2a"],"source_ids":["src_4075b6c35e0f503fac600b7ee3dc8a2f","src_acab5a616cbc5342920196d674bce990"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors are directed to read CONTRIBUTING.md before making changes, and AGENTS.md defines working rules for coding agents, runtime/data invariants, and Git handoff requirements.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_987e24a19f284983a8708d5f9149ef60"}
